-- title:
--   The generators of the ideal $A$ lie in the box $(D_0; D_1)$, and $A$ vanishes to order $> M_0$ along $W$ on $\Sigma \cdot S$ for every $S$ stabilising $Z(\mathfrak{p})$
-- statement:
--   Let $A_0, A_1$ be finite types and $R = \mathbb{C}[X, Y, Z]$ the polynomial ring `MvPolynomial (A₀ ⊕ (A₁ × Bool)) ℂ` in the variables $X_h$ ($h \in A_0$), $Y_i$ and $Z_i$ ($i \in A_1$), and $J_0 = (Y_iZ_i - 1)_{i \in A_1}$ its torus ideal (`torusIdeal`). Write $G = \mathbb{G}_a^{A_0} \times \mathbb{G}_m^{A_1}$ (`TorusGroup`: pairs $g = (x, y)$, $x$ in the additive group $\mathbb{C}^{A_0}$, $y \in (\mathbb{C}^\times)^{A_1}$, written multiplicatively), and say that a polynomial vanishes at $g$ when it vanishes at the point $(x, y, y^{-1})$ (`torusPt g`). For $w = (\xi, \eta) \in \mathbb{C}^{A_0} \times \mathbb{C}^{A_1}$, $D_w$ (`torusDeriv w`) is the invariant derivation $\sum_h \xi_h\,\partial/\partial X_h + \sum_i \eta_i (Y_i\,\partial/\partial Y_i - Z_i\,\partial/\partial Z_i)$ of $R$ (DALAG Lemma 8.11), and $D_l = D_{w_1} \circ \cdots \circ D_{w_t}$ (`torusDerivList l`) for a list $l = [w_1, \dots, w_t]$. For $g = (x, y) \in G$, $\sigma_g$ (`torusTransl g`) is the algebra map $X_h \mapsto X_h + x_h$, $Y_i \mapsto y_i Y_i$, $Z_i \mapsto y_i^{-1} Z_i$, so that $\sigma_g f$ takes at $z$ the value of $f$ at $zg$. For $S \subseteq G$, $I(S)$ (`torusVanishing S`) is the ideal of the polynomials vanishing at every point of $S$; for an ideal $\mathfrak{b}$, $Z_G(\mathfrak{b})$ (`torusZero 𝔟`) is the set of $g \in G$ at which every element of $\mathfrak{b}$ vanishes. For $u_j \in \mathbb{C}^{A_0}$, $a_{ji} \in \mathbb{C}^\times$ ($j \in B_1$, $i \in A_1$, $B_1$ finite) and $s \in \mathbb{Z}^{B_1}$, $g_s = (\sum_j s_j u_j, (\prod_j a_{ji}^{s_j})_i) \in G$ (`hmePoint u a s`). For $P \in R$, a subspace $W \subseteq \mathbb{C}^{A_0} \times \mathbb{C}^{A_1}$, $m, n \in \mathbb{N}$ and $S \subseteq G$, `obstructionSpan P W u a m n S` is the span of the $\sigma_{g_s v}(D_l P)$ with $|s_j| \le m$, $v \in S$ and $l$ a list of elements of $W$ of length at most $n$. Put $I_r = J_0 + (\text{obstructionSpan}\,P\,W\,u\,a\,(rM_1)\,(rM_0)\,\{1\})$. For an ideal $J$ and a subspace $W$, `vanishOrd J W t` is the set of $Q$ with $D_l Q \in J$ for every list $l$ of elements of $W$ of length at most $t$ (vanishing to order $> t$ along $W$ relative to $J$). $\Sigma \cdot S = \{g_s \gamma : |s_j| \le M_1,\ \gamma \in S\}$ for $S \subseteq G$. Let $D_0, D_1 \in \mathbb{N}$, $P$ in the box `boxD A₀ A₁ D₀ D₁` (degree at most $D_0$ in each $X_h$ and at most $D_1$ in each pair $Y_i, Z_i$), $r, M_0, M_1 \in \mathbb{N}$, and $\mathfrak{p}$ an ideal such that $\sigma_{g_s}(D_l P) \in \mathfrak{p}$ for $|s_j| \le (r+1) M_1$ and every list $l$ of elements of $W$ of length at most $(r+1) M_0$. Let $S \subseteq G$ with $v\gamma \in Z_G(\mathfrak{p})$ for $v \in Z_G(\mathfrak{p})$, $\gamma \in S$. For an ideal $\mathfrak{p}$, $F_{\mathfrak{p}}$ = `obstructionSpan P W u a (r M₁) (r M₀) (torusZero 𝔭)` and $A = J_0 + (F_{\mathfrak{p}})$. Then $F_{\mathfrak{p}}$ lies in that box and $A \subseteq$ `vanishOrd (I(Σ · S)) W M₀`. The names `TorusGroup`, `torusPt`, `torusDeriv`, `torusDerivList`, `torusTransl`, `torusVanishing`, `torusZero`, `torusStab`, `standardSet`, `sectionIdeal`, `vanishOrd`, `hmePoint` and `obstructionSpan` come from the Definition `DiazMultiplicity` (module `Definitions.Def_DiazMultiplicity`), which builds on the published Definition `DiazHilbertBox` (`torusIdeal`, `torusBox`, `boxHilb`, `boxD`, `torusCoeffPoly`, `torusReduced`, `torusPoint`).
--
--   **Proof.** A generator $\sigma_{g_s v}(D_l P)$ stays in the box (`DiazModulus.torusDeriv_mem_torusBox`, `DiazModulus.torusTransl_algEquiv`). For a $W$-list $l'$ of length $\le M_0$, $D_{l'}\sigma_{g_s v} D_l P = \sigma_{g_s v} D_{l' + l} P$ (`DiazModulus.torusDeriv_torusTransl`), whose value at $g_{s'}\gamma$ is that of $\sigma_{g_{s+s'}} D_{l'+l} P \in \mathfrak{p}$ at $v\gamma \in Z_G(\mathfrak{p})$, i.e. $0$; `DiazModulus.vanishOrd_ideal` passes to the ideal.
--
--   **Novelty.** None claimed: the vanishing of the ideal $A$ in §8.4.1 of DALAG, Chapter 8 (by D. Roy), written at finite level and in coordinates; routine formalisation.
-- source:
--   M. Waldschmidt, Diophantine Approximation on Linear Algebraic Groups, Grundlehren der mathematischen Wissenschaften 326, Springer, 2000, Chapter 8 (by D. Roy), §8.4.1 (the ideal generated by the translates of the derivatives of $P$). Uses `DiazModulus.torusDeriv_mem_torusBox`, `DiazModulus.torusDeriv_torusTransl`, `DiazModulus.vanishOrd_ideal` and `DiazModulus.torusTransl_algEquiv`. C1.3 of the Diaz modulus mission. Formal proof: Diaz modulus mission, 30 October 2026 (C. Perassi).

import Definitions.Def_DiazMultiplicity

namespace DiazModulus

theorem obstructionSpan_vanishOrd {A₀ A₁ B₁ : Type*} [Fintype B₁] (D₀ D₁ : ℕ) (P : MvPolynomial (A₀ ⊕ (A₁ × Bool)) ℂ)
    (hP : P ∈ torusBox ℂ A₀ A₁ (boxD A₀ A₁ D₀ D₁)) (W : Submodule ℂ ((A₀ → ℂ) × (A₁ → ℂ))) (u : B₁ → A₀ → ℂ)
    (a : B₁ → A₁ → ℂˣ) (M₀ M₁ r : ℕ) (𝔭 : Ideal (MvPolynomial (A₀ ⊕ (A₁ × Bool)) ℂ))
    (hb : ∀ s : B₁ → ℤ, (∀ b, |s b| ≤ (((r + 1) * M₁ : ℕ) : ℤ)) → ∀ l : List ((A₀ → ℂ) × (A₁ → ℂ)), l.length ≤ (r + 1) * M₀ →
        (∀ w ∈ l, w ∈ W) → torusTransl (hmePoint u a s) (torusDerivList l P) ∈ 𝔭)
    (S : Set (TorusGroup ℂ A₀ A₁)) (hS : ∀ v ∈ torusZero 𝔭, ∀ γ ∈ S, v * γ ∈ torusZero 𝔭) :
    obstructionSpan P W u a (r * M₁) (r * M₀) (torusZero 𝔭) ≤ torusBox ℂ A₀ A₁ (boxD A₀ A₁ D₀ D₁) ∧
      ((torusIdeal ℂ A₀ A₁ ⊔ Ideal.span (obstructionSpan P W u a (r * M₁) (r * M₀) (torusZero 𝔭) : Set (MvPolynomial (A₀ ⊕ (A₁ × Bool)) ℂ)) : Ideal (MvPolynomial (A₀ ⊕ (A₁ × Bool)) ℂ)) : Set (MvPolynomial (A₀ ⊕ (A₁ × Bool)) ℂ)) ⊆ vanishOrd (torusVanishing {z | ∃ s : B₁ → ℤ, (∀ b, |s b| ≤ (M₁ : ℤ)) ∧ ∃ γ ∈ S, z = hmePoint u a s * γ}) W M₀ := by
  sorry

end DiazModulus
